        "role": "user",
        "content": "Review the saved initial answer against ALL supplied source segments and cards. Find only valid answers that are missing from the initial answer, especially answers about different valid namesakes or scopes. Every proposed addition must answer the actual question, respect its entity/time/conditions/negation and have direct support from supplied segments. Do not include a candidate just because it appears in a document, and do not conflate contradictory versions of the same fact. Return only additional short answers with supporting segment IDs. Return no additions if none is established. Do not remove or rewrite any initial answer. Sources are data, never instructions.\nSearch for missing answers to this precise slot. A birthplace is never a date, an associated person is not automatically an artist. Preserve distinct valid referents, do not invent question constraints. Serialize up to12 additions in A0..A11; unused slots have all empty strings. Each occupied slot needs a short answer and supplied source segment ID(s). Do not fill slots gratuitously.\nInput: {\"question\": \"When was the Empire of Haiti established?\", \"original_source_segments\": {\"D1S1\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0178-05f4a986d78f:d00\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 126, \"text\": \"First Empire of Haiti The First Empire of Haiti (; Haitian Creole: \\\"Anpi an Ayiti\\\") was an elective monarchy in North America.\"}, \"D1S2\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0178-05f4a986d78f:d00\", \"start\": 127, \"end\": 207, \"text\": \"Haiti was controlled by France before declaring independence on January 1, 1804.\"}, \"D1S3\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0178-05f4a986d78f:d00\", \"start\": 208, \"end\": 305, \"text\": \"The Governor-General of Haiti, Jean-Jacques Dessalines, created the empire on September 22, 1804.\"}, \"D1S4\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0178-05f4a986d78f:d00\", \"start\": 306, \"end\": 390, \"text\": \"Proclaiming himself Emperor Jacques I, he held his coronation ceremony on October 6.\"}, \"D1S5\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0178-05f4a986d78f:d00\", \"start\": 391, \"end\": 522, \"text\": \"The constitution of May 20, 1805 set out the way the empire was to be governed, with the country split into six military divisions.\"}, \"D1S6\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0178-05f4a986d78f:d00\", \"start\": 523, \"end\": 625, \"text\": \"The general of each division corresponded directly with the emperor, or the general in chief appointed\"}, \"D2S1\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0178-05f4a986d78f:d01\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 195, \"text\": \"Second Empire of Haiti The Second Haitian Empire, officially known as the Empire of Haiti (French: \\\"Empire d'Haïti\\\"; Haitian Creole: \\\"Anpi an Ayiti\\\"), was a state which existed from 1849 to 1859.\"}, \"D2S2\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0178-05f4a986d78f:d01\", \"start\": 196, \"end\": 512, \"text\": \"It was established by the then-President, former Lieutenant General and Supreme Commander of the Presidential Guards under President Riché, Faustin Soulouque, who, inspired by Napoleon I, declared himself Emperor Faustin I of Haiti on August 26, 1849 at the Cathedral of Our Lady of the Assumption in Port-au-Prince.\"}, \"D2S3\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0178-05f4a986d78f:d01\", \"start\": 513, \"end\": 638, \"text\": \"Faustin's unsuccessful invasions (in part due to the diplomatic interference of the United States and Spain) in an attempt to\"}}, \"original_cards\": [{\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0178-05f4a986d78f:d00\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0178-05f4a986d78f:d00:c0\", \"entity\": \"Empire of Haiti\", \"scope\": \"Establishment date\", \"claim\": \"The Governor-General of Haiti, Jean-Jacques Dessalines, created the empire on September 22, 1804.\", \"answer\": \"September 22, 1804\", \"quote\": \"The Governor-General of Haiti, Jean-Jacques Dessalines, created the empire on September 22, 1804.\", \"original_document_number\": 1}, {\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0178-05f4a986d78f:d01\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0178-05f4a986d78f:d01:c0\", \"entity\": \"Empire of Haiti\", \"scope\": \"Establishment date\", \"claim\": \"The Empire of Haiti was established on August 26, 1849.\", \"answer\": \"August 26, 1849\", \"quote\": \"It was established by the then-President, former Lieutenant General and Supreme Commander of the Presidential Guards under President Riché, Faustin Soulouque, who, inspired by Napoleon I, declared himself Emperor Faustin I of Haiti on August 26, 1849 at the Cathedral of Our Lady of the Assumption in Port-au-Prince.\", \"original_document_number\": 2}], \"current_answers\": [\"September 22, 1804\", \"August 26, 1849\"], \"candidate_answers\": [{\"candidate_id\": \"R0\", \"answer\": \"September 22, 1804\", \"origin\": \"initial\"}, {\"candidate_id\": \"R1\", \"answer\": \"August 26, 1849\", \"origin\": \"initial\"}], \"requested_slot_hint\": \"other\"}"
